    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0d0cb164-3cf3-56d7-995f-ef859d8ceb0a",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 8 & 10 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 0 & -24 \\\\ -55 & 0 & -46 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{32}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 8 & 10 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+3R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 0 & -24 \\\\ -7 & 8 & 10 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}+8R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 0 & -24 \\\\ -55 & 0 & -46 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+3R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}+8R_{3}$.",
