      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 2 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 50 & 39 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 11 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{31}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 2 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 50 & 39 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-2R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 50 & 39 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 11 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -5\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-6R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-2R_{3}$.",
